# Asynchronous Fraud Detection API Using Flask and Redis

## 1. Project Overview

This task involved implementing Redis result storage and retrieval for an asynchronous fraud-detection scoring system developed for xFusionCorp Industries.

The application uses Flask as its HTTP entry point. Prediction requests are processed by a background worker so that the HTTP endpoint can return a task ID without waiting for the model prediction to finish.

Redis is used to persist completed prediction results, allowing clients to retrieve them through a separate HTTP endpoint.

